-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 9, עובדי הוראה המלמדים הנדסאים וטכנאים
-- Teachers of practical engineers and technicians (classes 13-14): group
-- size, the work unit by degree, the school year, hiring, the roles they may
-- hold, and the division principal and deputies with their allowances.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `9 עובדי הוראה המלמדים הנדסאים וטכנאים`

§§ `9.1 תנאי עבודה`

§§§ `9.1.1 קבוצת עבודה`

@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_1/p1
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `students in a work group` IS 12

DECLARE `group-size action` IS ONE OF
    `enlarge a work group beyond 12`
    `refer the enlargement to the joint committee`

-- Enlarging a group past 12 is brought to a joint committee of the ministry,
-- the owners and the teachers' representatives: read as a duty to refer
-- before enlarging. Time in school months.
@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_1/p2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `group-size action`
DECIDE `an enlargement goes to the joint committee` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `refer the enlargement to the joint committee`
    WITHIN 1
    HENCE (PARTY `the local authority or owning body` MAY `enlarge a work group beyond 12`)
    LEST  (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
           SHANT `enlarge a work group beyond 12`
           WITHIN 12
           LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 9.1.1: a group above 12 students must first go to the joint committee")

§§§ `9.1.2 יחידת עבודה`

@desc The degrees section 9.1.2 sets a work unit for, as printed.
DECLARE `degree` IS ONE OF
    `technician`                       @desc תואר טכנאי
    `practical engineer`               @desc תואר הנדסאי
    `BA`                               @desc ב"א
    `BSc in engineering`               @desc ב"ס בהנדסה
    `MA or MSc`                        @desc מ"א או מ"ס
    `doctorate`                        @desc ד"ר
    `BSc outside engineering`          @desc a first degree the list does not name (F-9-a)
    `engineer`                         @desc the title מהנדס, which section 9.10 names and 9.1.2 does not

@desc One row of section 9.1.2: the work unit for a degree, before and after two years of teaching in classes 13-14.
DECLARE `work-unit row` HAS
    `row degree`                IS A `degree`
    `weekly hours`              IS A NUMBER
    `weekly hours after two years` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_2__subpara_a
`row a` MEANS `work-unit row` `technician` 21 21
@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_2__subpara_b
`row b` MEANS `work-unit row` `practical engineer` 21 21
@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_2__subpara_c akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_2__subpara_c/p2
`row c` MEANS `work-unit row` `BA` 21 20
@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_2__subpara_d akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_2__subpara_d/p2
`row d` MEANS `work-unit row` `BSc in engineering` 20 19
@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_2__subpara_e akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_2__subpara_e/p2
`row e` MEANS `work-unit row` `MA or MSc` 19 18
@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_2__subpara_f akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_2__subpara_f/p2
`row f` MEANS `work-unit row` `doctorate` 18 17

@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_2/p1
`the work-unit table` MEANS LIST `row a`, `row b`, `row c`, `row d`, `row e`, `row f`

GIVEN d IS A `degree`
GIVETH A LIST OF `work-unit row`
DECIDE `the rows for` d IS
    filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row degree` EQUALS d) `the work-unit table`

-- F-9-a: a first degree the list does not name has no row. The reading
-- adopted gives it the BA row (any first degree other than a BSc in
-- engineering); an engineer's title is read with the BSc in engineering.
GIVEN d IS A `degree`
GIVETH A `degree`
DECIDE `the row a degree is read under` d IS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `BSc outside engineering` THEN `BA`
    WHEN `engineer`                THEN `BSc in engineering`
    OTHERWISE d

GIVEN d IS A `degree`, `years teaching classes 13-14` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `work unit` d `years teaching classes 13-14` IS
    CONSIDER `the rows for` (`the row a degree is read under` d)
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF `years teaching classes 13-14` AT LEAST 2
        THEN r's `weekly hours after two years`
        ELSE r's `weekly hours`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0

`a BSc outside engineering has no row` MEANS
    `the rows for` `BSc outside engineering` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `a BSc outside engineering has no row`

-- Every printed degree has exactly one row.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD count (`the rows for` d) EQUALS 1)
            (LIST `technician`, `practical engineer`, `BA`, `BSc in engineering`, `MA or MSc`, `doctorate`)

§§§ `9.1.3 שנת הלימודים`

-- F-9-b: whether the 30 weeks bind every programme or only the adult
-- schools the sentence ends with. Reading adopted: 30 net weeks for all,
-- and the 5 exam weeks in the adult schools only.
@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1__para_3/p1
GIVEN `adult school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks in the school year` `adult school` IS
    IF `adult school`
    THEN 30 PLUS 5
    ELSE 30

GIVEN `adult school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks in the school year if the whole sentence speaks of adult schools` `adult school` IS
    IF `adult school`
    THEN 30 PLUS 5
    ELSE 0

`the two readings of 9.1.3 differ for a programme that is not an adult school` MEANS
    NOT (`weeks in the school year` FALSE
         EQUALS `weeks in the school year if the whole sentence speaks of adult schools` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the two readings of 9.1.3 differ for a programme that is not an adult school`

-- akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1/p1 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1/p2 Source: a director-general's circular.
-- akn:chp_9__ssec_9_1/p3 Source: a director-general's circular.

§§ `9.2 קבלה לעבודה`

@desc A candidate to teach practical engineers and technicians.
DECLARE `candidate teacher` HAS
    `holds at least a first degree`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a technician or practical-engineer title` IS A BOOLEAN
    `special approval of the head of technological education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the special approval the exception requires

@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_2/p1 akn:chp_9__ssec_9_2/p2
GIVEN c IS A `candidate teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be appointed to teach practical engineers and technicians` c IF
        c's `holds at least a first degree`
    OR (    c's `holds a technician or practical-engineer title`
        AND c's `special approval of the head of technological education`)

-- akn:chp_9__ssec_9_2/p3 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_9__ssec_9_2/p4 Source: a director-general's circular and a clarification.

§§ `9.6 גמולים`

@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_6/p1 akn:chp_9__ssec_9_6__para_1 akn:chp_9__ssec_9_6__para_2
DECLARE `role open to a teacher of classes 13-14` IS ONE OF
    `class educator`
    `subject coordinator`
    `laboratory coordinator`
    `pedagogical-centre or teaching-aids coordinator`

-- akn:chp_9__ssec_9_6__para_2/p2 A pointer to section 1.12 for the roles' details and allowances, encoded there.
-- akn:chp_9__ssec_9_6/p2 Heading of an empty source list (אסמכתא).

§§ `9.10 מנהל`

@desc An institution with classes 13-14 for practical engineers and technicians.
DECLARE `technological institution` HAS
    `classes 13 and 14`            IS A NUMBER @desc classes 13 and 14 for practical engineers and technicians (or first- and second-year classes in an adult school)
    `post-primary allowance rate for that number of classes` IS A NUMBER
        @desc the management allowance of a post-primary school principal for that number of classes, from section 7.6.6.1's table; an input until that table is encoded

DECLARE `appointment action` IS ONE OF
    `appoint a division principal` HAS `the appointee's degree` IS A `degree`
    `appoint a deputy` HAS `which deputy` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_10__para_1__subpara_a
GIVEN i IS A `technological institution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a division principal must be appointed` i IF
    i's `classes 13 and 14` GREATER THAN 3

@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_10__para_1__subpara_b
GIVEN d IS A `degree`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds a degree a division principal needs` d IF
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `engineer`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `MA or MSc` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `doctorate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "ימונה" is passive and names no appointing body; the owners, who
-- employ the staff of a post-primary institution (section 7.6.3.2(15)), are
-- read as the party the duty falls on, here and in section 9.11.
GIVEN i IS A `technological institution`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `appointment action`
DECIDE `appointing the division principal` i IS
    IF `a division principal must be appointed` i
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `appoint a division principal` d PROVIDED `holds a degree a division principal needs` d
         WITHIN 12
         LEST  BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 9.10.1: an institution with more than three classes 13-14 has a division principal, holding one of the degrees named"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_10__para_2/p1
GIVEN i IS A `technological institution`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `division principal's management allowance rate` i IS
    0.85 TIMES i's `post-primary allowance rate for that number of classes`

-- akn:chp_9__ssec_9_10/p1 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_9__ssec_9_10/p2 Source: a director-general's circular.

§§ `9.11 סגן מנהל`

@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_11__para_1__subpara_a
GIVEN i IS A `technological institution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a first deputy may be appointed` i IF
    i's `classes 13 and 14` AT LEAST 8

@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_11__para_1__subpara_b
GIVEN i IS A `technological institution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a second deputy must be appointed` i IF
    i's `classes 13 and 14` AT LEAST 15

GIVEN i IS A `technological institution`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `appointment action`
DECIDE `appointing deputies` i IS
    IF `a second deputy must be appointed` i
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `appoint a deputy` n PROVIDED n EQUALS 2
         WITHIN 12
         LEST  BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 9.11.1(b): a school of 15 classes or more has a second deputy"
    ELSE IF `a first deputy may be appointed` i
         THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
              MAY   `appoint a deputy` n PROVIDED n EQUALS 1
              WITHIN 12
         ELSE FULFILLED

-- The deputies are appointed, and given management hours, within the
-- existing quota of management hours: the hours given to deputies may not
-- push the institution past its quota.
@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_11__para_1__subpara_c
GIVEN `management hours already used` IS A NUMBER, `hours given to the deputies` IS A NUMBER,
      `management-hours quota` IS A NUMBER @desc the institution's existing quota of management hours; an input
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deputies fit the existing quota` `management hours already used` `hours given to the deputies` `management-hours quota` IF
    `management hours already used` PLUS `hours given to the deputies` AT MOST `management-hours quota`

-- The deputy's allowance follows the general rules of the management
-- allowance and the number of classes 13-14; its rate comes from a table
-- (in force from 1.9.95) that is not part of the text this file encodes.
@ref akn:chp_9__ssec_9_11__para_2/p1
GIVEN `deputy's table rate` IS A NUMBER @desc the percentage the deputies' table gives for the institution's classes 13-14; an input
      `personal combined salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `deputy's management allowance` `deputy's table rate` `personal combined salary` IS
    `deputy's table rate` TIMES `personal combined salary`

-- akn:chp_9__ssec_9_11/p1 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_9__ssec_9_11/p2 Source: a director-general's circular and the collective agreement of 23.12.90.
-- akn:chp_9__ssec_9_11/p3 Source: collective agreement of 11.5.93.
-- akn:chp_9__ssec_9_11/p4 Source: a director-general's circular.

-- Examples. The post-primary rate of 10 is a placeholder.
`an institution with 16 classes 13-14` MEANS
    `technological institution` WITH
        `classes 13 and 14` IS 16
        `post-primary allowance rate for that number of classes` IS 10

#ASSERT `division principal's management allowance rate` `an institution with 16 classes 13-14` EQUALS 8.5
#ASSERT `work unit` `MA or MSc` 3 EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `work unit` `technician` 5 EQUALS 21
#EVAL   `work unit` `BSc outside engineering` 0

#TRACE `appointing the division principal` `an institution with 16 classes 13-14` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `appoint a division principal` `MA or MSc` AT 1
#TRACE `appointing the division principal` `an institution with 16 classes 13-14` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `appoint a division principal` `BA` AT 1
#TRACE `appointing deputies` `an institution with 16 classes 13-14` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `appoint a deputy` 2 AT 1
